OL,3,GNEWSACar park deal paves way for 1,000
OL,4,Acity centre homes
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council is set to pay #750,000
OL,7,Ftowards the cost of buying a 24-hour
OL,8,Fcar park as part of plans to build more
OL,9,Fthan 1,000 homes in the city centre.
OL,11,FThe purchase of the former Network
OL,12,FHouse site on School Street,
OL,13,FWolverhampton, will make way for the
OL,14,FSmithgate development, which will also
OL,15,Ffeature a mix of public spaces, shops
OL,16,Fand restaurants.
OL,18,FThe site was recently listed for sale
OL,19,Fwith a #2.1m asking price and the City
OL,20,Fof Wolverhampton Council has agreed to
OL,21,Fsplit the cost with developer English
OL,22,FCities Fund (ECF).
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
